<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<assembly manifestVersion="1.0" xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v1">

  <!--
    中文：
      本清单只做两件事，两件都与规格挂钩。

      1. requestedExecutionLevel = asInvoker —— 绝不提权（规格 §2.1 假设 A2）。
         业务软件是普通权限的浏览器。若本工具以管理员身份运行，UIPI 会让它
         既看不到浏览器的按键、也无法向浏览器发送输入——整个用户态架构当场
         失效，而且失效得很安静：程序照常运行，就是什么都收不到。

      2. dpiAware / dpiAwareness —— 声明 PerMonitorV2（规格 §18 要求支持
         100%、125%、150% 缩放）。不声明的话 Windows 会对窗口做位图拉伸，
         界面发虚，而且拿到的窗口坐标是虚拟化过的，与规格 §11.5 "校验存储的
         坐标是否落在可见屏幕内" 对不上。
    English:
      This manifest does two things, both tied to the spec.

      1. asInvoker — never elevate (spec §2.1, assumption A2). The business
         application is an unelevated browser. Running elevated would have UIPI block
         this tool from both observing the browser's keystrokes and sending input to
         it — the entire user-mode architecture fails, and fails quietly: the program
         runs normally and simply receives nothing.

      2. PerMonitorV2 DPI awareness (spec §18 requires 100%, 125% and 150% scaling).
         Without it Windows bitmap-stretches the window, blurring it and handing back
         virtualized coordinates that do not match spec §11.5's requirement to
         validate stored coordinates against the visible desktop.
  -->

  <trustInfo xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v2">
    <security>
      <requestedPrivileges xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v3">
        <requestedExecutionLevel level="asInvoker" uiAccess="false" />
      </requestedPrivileges>
    </security>
  </trustInfo>

  <compatibility xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:compatibility.v1">
    <application>
      <!-- Windows 10 / 11 -->
      <supportedOS Id="{8e0f7a12-bfb3-4fe8-b9a5-48fd50a15a9a}" />
    </application>
  </compatibility>

  <application xmlns="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:asm.v3">
    <windowsSettings>
      <dpiAware xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/SMI/2005/WindowsSettings">true/pm</dpiAware>
      <dpiAwareness xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/SMI/2016/WindowsSettings">permonitorv2</dpiAwareness>
    </windowsSettings>
  </application>

</assembly>
